# Cordova plugins for Capacitor
capacitor-cordova-ios-plugins

# Generated Config files
#
# `App/App/capacitor.config.json`, `App/App/config.xml` and `App/App/public/` are
# normally ignored because `npx cap sync ios` regenerates them. They are committed here
# on purpose: App.xcodeproj references all three from its Resources build phase, so
# without them Xcode fails the build. Committing them makes `ios/App/App.xcodeproj`
# buildable straight after a fresh `git clone`, with no Node toolchain and no
# `cap sync` step — the remaining dependency (capacitor-swift-pm) is a remote SPM
# package Xcode resolves on its own.
#
# They stay generated artefacts: re-run `pnpm cap:sync` after changing
# `capacitor.config.ts` or `capacitor/www/`, and commit the result.
